.SS "\fBAttributes\fP clipOverflow (boolean clip)"

.PP
Confine drawing overflow to the operation's bounds\&. Defaults to false\&. When true, the operation temporarily intersects the current \fBPort\fP clip with its transformed axis-aligned bounds, restoring the \fBPort\fP clip on return\&. False allows operation overflow but never disables the \fBPort\fP clip\&.

.PP
Bounds are the supplied rectangle, quad or polygon bounds for closed shapes; the ellipse or sphere bounding rectangle; measured text bounds for point text; the supplied rectangle for rectangle text; and \fBDrawing\fP geometry bounds mapped into the requested destination for \fBDrawing\fP replay\&. Line and spline bounds include half the stroke width in \fBPort\fP pixels, so horizontal and vertical paths remain visible; arc bounds use their ellipse with the same stroke allowance\&. Other closed-shape bounds exclude the outer half of their stroke\&. Bounds follow translation, rotation, scaling and reflection as an axis-aligned enclosing rectangle\&.

.PP
Images and image strips also crop fitted artwork to the destination before its transform, including rotated destinations, subsection/frame selection and all fit modes\&. fit_Clipped always crops; tiling crops partial edge tiles\&. Nested \fBDrawing\fP replay respects its enclosing operation clip without exposing a public clip stack\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIclip\fP True to clip overflow; false to allow it within the \fBPort\fP clip\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This \fBAttributes\fP object, for chaining\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBPort::setClipRect()\fP, \fBPort::resetClipRect()\fP 
.RE
.PP

